{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>אֲשֶׁר נָתַן לִי וְגוֹ׳.</b> It is the way of the righteous that when they recall the good that has come to them, they ascribe honor to HaShem, for He is the Giver, as he said (Genesis 33:5): ״הַיְלָדִים אֲשֶׁר חָנַן אֱלֹהִים״ and so forth." "And the verse's saying <b>בָּזֶה</b> — according to the plain sense, it means that even during the days of his exile in a foreign land, HaShem granted him children. He also alluded to the statement of our Sages of blessed memory (Sotah 36b) that Yosef was destined to beget twelve tribes, but through the incident of Potiphar's wife, ten drops were diminished from between his fingernails and only two remained. And this is what he alluded to by saying <b>בָּזֶה</b> — ״זֶה״ in gematria is twelve; in place of twelve, Elohim gave him two. He was precise in saying <b>אֱלֹהִים</b>, which indicates judgment."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 48, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:50:05.766369948Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}